target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestDecide'
expect: unknown (review not finished)
why:    the zero value of a string is not a convergence word. An unset Convergence must read as unknown and owe the disclosure, never fall into the converged branch: `unknown` is what a run with no cycle rows derives, and it is the cheapest state to produce.
--- old
	conv := s.Convergence
	if conv == "" {
		conv = record.Unknown
	}
--- new
	conv := s.Convergence
